# Example env rows for the feat `req` feature (spec: feat/back/spec/req.md), mounted via
# the backend-slots loader (spec: feat/back/spec/backend-slots.md).
# The _MOUNT row is the slot config: present = feature attached at that path, absent = dormant.
# Recipes = FEAT_REQ_<NAME>_*; presence of _TARGET enables the route <mount>/<name>.
# ${UPPER_SNAKE} references resolve from the env first — shared values live in one row.
# Reference recipe: retrigger a project's last serf deploy run via flow /retrigger.
# {{project}} is filled from the caller's param (public by contract — no secrets there).
FLOW_BACK_URL=https://flow-back-host
FEAT_REQ_MOUNT=/req
FEAT_REQ_RETRIGGER_TARGET=${FLOW_BACK_URL}/retrigger
FEAT_REQ_RETRIGGER_METHOD=post
FEAT_REQ_RETRIGGER_HEADERS={"Authorization": "Bearer <APP_TRIGGER_RUN_TOKEN>"}
FEAT_REQ_RETRIGGER_BODY={"project": "{{project}}"}
# feat features (specs: feat/back/spec/*.md) — loader v3 named slots. The SLOT row is
# the toggle (absent = dormant, no route); WHO fills a slot is this config, WHERE the
# slot sits is host code. `route` is the built-in HTTP-endpoint slot; the canonical
# path comes from the feature itself (defaultMount) — _MOUNT only overrides it.
# FEAT_GET_UPDATES_SLOT=route
# FEAT_REQ_SLOT=route
# feat host for loader remote resolution (v2.1): features without a vendored copy are
# fetched from here at boot (manifest latest → js-node main file). Set together with the
# feature's _MOUNT row in the deploy env; nothing is written into this repo.
# FEAT_URL=https://feat.twc1.net
